    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_7b31500730524e4ebf2cdf50ce1025d71215bb1dfe1819a11f3399dfdb3cea20",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Nonintersecting Brownian motion, structured tridiagonal products, and Haar-random unitary matrices can be treated as alternative generators once they induce the same circular β=2 point-process law. For calculations that use the joint zero statistics, that law is the invariant content and the generating matrix is not privileged; historical eigenvalue language should not be mistaken for a claim that every realization literally comes from a matrix.",
