    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fbe13b4964d780ae9455338cd9ddd2e6ceb4540f5f2327be6e37f8f7aa25994c",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source redirects Blanc's proposed contradiction into an inverse gap problem: a most-likely compressed neighbor profile determines interpolation weights, repeated differentiation regularizes that geometry toward cosine spacing, and comparison with a zeta-specific high-derivative bound may turn resistance to regularization into an upper bound on gap size.",
